From: iPool bring-up <dev@ipool>
Date: Mon, 28 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip-inno-dsidphy: retarget LVDS PLL for the SZ3568 panel

The inno-dsidphy LVDS mode hardcodes the PLL divider as prediv=2,
fbdiv=28. With the driver's PLL formula fout = fbdiv * (ref/2) / prediv
and ref = 24 MHz, that is 28 * 12MHz / 2 = 168 MHz bit clock, i.e. a
168/7 = 24 MHz pixel clock (7:1 LVDS serialization).

24 MHz is below the minimum pixel clock of the iPool SZ3568's 7"
1024x600 LVDS panel (XXR070B4120), so the panel never locks: the
backlight is on but the image is black.

Use prediv=1 (keeping fbdiv=28): 28 * 12MHz / 1 = 336 MHz bit clock ->
336/7 = 48.0 MHz pixel. That exact rate is matched by the VOP2 pixel
clock (dclk_vp1 = GPLL 1200/25 = 48 MHz, set via the board DT) and the
panel timing, so the LVDS link locks.

This is a board-specific downstream hack for a single fixed panel; the
proper upstream fix would compute the PLL from the requested mode clock.

Downstream (meta-ipool) fix for the RK3568 SZ3568 board.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific hardcode; upstream needs mode-derived PLL]
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c
@@ -526,7 +526,14 @@

 static void inno_dsidphy_lvds_mode_enable(struct inno_dsidphy *inno)
 {
-	u8 prediv = 2;
+	/*
+	 * meta-ipool: upstream default prediv=2,fbdiv=28 gives
+	 * 28*12MHz/2 = 168MHz bit clock = 168/7 = 24MHz pixel, below our
+	 * 1024x600 panel's min -> never locks (black). Use prediv=1 ->
+	 * 28*12/1 = 336MHz -> 336/7 = 48.0MHz pixel, matched exactly by
+	 * dclk_vp1 (GPLL 1200/25 = 48MHz, see &vop) and the panel timing.
+	 */
+	u8 prediv = 1;
 	u16 fbdiv = 28;

 	/* Sample clock reverse direction */
